WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.333
[music]

2
00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:09.466
[Instructor] Cool, so, we have this
cool smoke explosion

3
00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:11.400
here that we can Play,

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.366
but one of the things we need
to do is actually make it Play

5
00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:18.133
when the Player runs into
one of our Obstacles.

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.533
So If I time it right, [explosion]

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.333
so something like that, pretty close.
The computer can probably do

8
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.700
it better than I can
so we'll just have the computer do it.

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.400
So we can actually do that by going

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.400
into our PlayerController Script.

11
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.433
And then in our PlayerController Script,

12
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.366
very similar to how we got
our Components

13
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.933
for our Rigidbody and our Animator,

14
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:42.200
we'll do something similar.

15
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.866
In this case,
because our Particle System

16
00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:47.033
is actually outside

17
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.700
of our Player Components

18
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.300
we'll make this a "public...

19
00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:54.600
ParticleSystem..."

20
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.733
And we'll call
this the "explosionParticle."

21
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:05.066
So now this'll create
one of those variables

22
00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:06.933
in our Component that we
need to drag

23
00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.100
something on to.
So we'll do that later.

24
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.700
Now in our PlayerController
if() statement

25
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:16.333
whenever a Player runs into an Obstacle

26
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:18.400
this is where we're actually
going to make

27
00:01:18.866 --> 00:01:20.866
our explosionParticle happen.

28
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:25.366
So, when the Player dies,
we can add another line,

29
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.133
and we have the explosionParticle now,

30
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.400
and we can actually

31
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.066
just "Play()" the Particle.

32
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.666
And so that entire animation
Effect will just play

33
00:01:37.966 --> 00:01:40.066
as soon as it hits this line of code.

34
00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:44.400
So, we run into an Obstacle,
Game Over happens, Player dies,

35
00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:47.833
and it'll Play the explosion
Effect that we have.

36
00:01:48.266 --> 00:01:50.466
And then, in Unity,

37
00:01:50.766 --> 00:01:53.833
just make sure that when you go
to your Player Object

38
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.533
you take your explosion smoke,

39
00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.066
and drag it down
to the PlayerController Script,

40
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.200
and drop it into the Explosion Particle.

41
00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:06.333
So now, when we press Play...

42
00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:10.833
when the Player runs into an Obstacle

43
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:12.833
we should see a big puff of smoke.

44
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.000
Perfect, that's exactly
what we were looking for.

45
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.400
So, now what you're going to do,

46
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.300
is in your PlayerController Script,

47
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.433
you're going to create a public
variable that is a Particle System,

48
00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:27.433
and we'll call it explosion Particle.

49
00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.800
And then in our OnCollisionEnter()
method,

50
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.966
where we actually end the game
by running into an Obstacle,

51
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:38.533
we're just going to call 
that explosionParticle variable,

52
00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:41.033
and Play it so it Plays the animation.

53
00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:45.233
And then, in Unity,
just make sure to click and drag

54
00:02:45.233 --> 00:02:48.066
on your explosion smoke
in your Hierarchy,

55
00:02:48.866 --> 00:02:52.666
drop it into the Particle
in your PlayerController Script,

56
00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.366
and then when you Play the game, 
and run it you should see

57
00:02:55.366 --> 00:02:57.700
a big puff of smoke when you run
into an Obstacle.

58
00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.400
Now it's your turn.

59
00:03:00.466 --> 00:03:03.100
[music]
